QA,

Please open an investigation for a near miss in synthesis bay 3. No deviation number has been assigned. I am the production manager on days.

Product: omeprazole sulfide intermediate
Batch: OMP-INT-26-077
Process stage: solvent charge
Equipment: reactor R-210
Site: Northline API Works, Hyderabad, synthesis bay 3

At 15:41 today the warehouse operator overrode a barcode mismatch on scanner WH-SCN-2. The drum staged at the charging booth was methanol drum MD-4418. The batch record calls for ethanol drum ED-2201. The override reason code was left blank. The operator used a supervisor login; I have not yet confirmed whose credentials those were. Badge activity at the booth shows K. Das in the area, but I cannot say from this email that K. Das performed the override.

Line clearance checklist LC-OMP-INT for bay 3 was signed by S. Kulkarni at 15:10, before the methanol drum was moved to the booth. The checklist marks the solvent staging area as clear.

The charging step has not started. No material was added to reactor R-210. Drum MD-4418 was returned to the methanol cage and tagged "do not use — staging error 18 Mar 2026". The ethanol drum ED-2201 is still in the ethanol store and was not opened.

Impact as I see it: no product was contacted, the batch can continue once QA agrees the booth is clear, and nothing has left the site. This would have been a wrong-solvent charge had the override not been noticed by the bay chemist at the pre-charge check.

What I still need from the investigation:
- the scanner audit trail for WH-SCN-2 at 15:41, including the user id on the override
- whether the methanol label on MD-4418 was legible (the operator told the chemist the label was faded, but I have not seen it)
- why line clearance was signed at 15:10 if the drum arrived later
- whether override-with-blank-reason is even allowed by warehouse SOP WH-SOP-006

I have paused the charge. The batch is not on deviation status in the system because we do not have a number.

